gbm: buffers in AHardwareBuffers from the DroidNux display server

With DROIDNUX_AHB_SOCKET set, linear BGRA buffers come from the
allocator the app runs (display/src/main/cpp/core/allocator.h in
DroidNux), imported as dma-bufs, so a nested compositor's frames reach
Android's compositor as they are. Rows are added for Turnip's linear
layout (4-row alignment, 4 KiB size alignment).

